An experiment on an isolated nerve-muscle preparation shows that drug P has the following effects on a single stimulation of the motor nerve:

- the quantity of acetylcholine released from the knob is unchanged;
- $\mathrm{Ca^{2+}}$ entry into the knob is unchanged;
- the depolarisation of the muscle fibre membrane is larger and lasts much longer than normal.

Which is the most likely action of drug P?
